A||||6||jeffndebrus||aurora (northstar) 4.0 32 valve||||1||
Z||000000||jeffndebrus||11-07-2001||08:00 PM||||I have access to a new crated 4.0 32 valve (aurora) northstar.<P>1)which transmission should I use?(my 85 se is auto)<P>2)where to find engine mounts?<P>3)what is the main cost of this swap?<P>4)can I use my existing axles?<P>5)atherd(BEN) already showed me a site to find electronics-any more?<P>6)any input is always appreciated!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-07-2001||08:14 PM||||Depends, do you want to retain the auto or go manual?  If you go auto, you have to change axles, hubs, spindle, rotors and calipers and rear bolt pattern on rims.  That is not a bad thing. <BR> Are you going to do the work yourself or send it out?  My Northstar has no bushings.  It is solid mounted to a customized cradle and custom tranny brackets.  It is smooth as silk, after all it is a caddy engine (Aurora is the same).  My total conversion cost me unde $8 000 Canadian.  That includes rims, rubber, engine, tranny, hoses, clamps, hubs, lowering springs, rotors, calipers, leather interior, digital gauges, custom wiring harness and a cadillac Cluster,ecm and prom.  Basically everything.  Howel engine developements uses an Aurora harness for the Northstar, they may be able to help you.  The guys name to speak to is Troy.  The number is on my web page <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jeffndebrus||11-07-2001||09:02 PM||||I was thinking of doing the swap myself Jay.<BR>I don't know if that is a good idea or not?<BR>If I go with a manual tranny which one would I use and would that actually be easier?<BR>If I stay with auto should I not upgrade to a four speed auto??<BR>Any idea how much 8,000 canadian dollars mean in us funds (excuse my ignorance)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-07-2001||09:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Any idea how much 8,000 canadian dollars mean in us funds <HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That would be $5,020.08 USD,as of noon today.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||11-07-2001||09:37 PM||||Go manual if you possible can. DOHC engines work especially well with manuals. If you want to keep the auto, you are just as well off with a 3.8SC.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||11-08-2001||05:19 PM||||If you go auto, then use the Aurora tranny that is ment for the engine, alot easier to run with the stock ecm, and you won't have to modify it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-08-2001||11:44 PM||||Auroras are rear drive however, so you can't use the stock tranny at all...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com</A>  will set you up with a running engine (with their computer and harness) from there, the motor WILL BOLT UP to any Fiero manual tranny with some minor moding.<P>I'd recomend a Getrag or Isuzu 5-speed tranny wise. Stay away from autos, they'll be a big old mess making them work.<P>Oh clutch wise, you can get an 88 Fiero flywheel re-drilled for the Northstar/Aurora pattern, and it will work fine! (the mating surfaces are already in the right place, go GM!)<P>Be prepared to get down and dirty with a soldering iron, a MIG welder, and a local hardware store  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   But you can do it yourself.<P>Stock tranny mount locations can be used (though I recomend you 'box in' the rubber mounts with steel, making a set of solid mounts.)  the only one you will have to fab is the front engine mount.  And it won't be hard.  Honest!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Grab a fuel pump from a '96 Corvette.  Has plenty of flow, and the right pressure!<P>Expect it to cost around $5k if you're really clever.   More if you put Aeroquip fittings on everything, and are nutty-obsessive about details  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>If you go auto, then use the Aurora tranny that is ment for the engine, alot easier to run with the stock ecm, and you won't have to modify it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
